---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site, url } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="John T. Campbell Jr. on building software, leading engineering teams, and exploring agentic development."
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <div class="eyebrow">04 / ABOUT</div>
    <h1>
      Still building.
      <br />
      Still asking questions<span class="accent">.</span>
    </h1>
  </header>
  <div class="page-content about-grid">
    <article class="prose">
      <p>
        I've been building software professionally since before “the web” needed
        a qualifier.
      </p>
      <p>
        That work has taken me from software development into architecture,
        engineering leadership, and security engineering. I've built software
        systems, engineering teams, and technology organizations. Each chapter
        has changed the scale of the problems, but not my interest in
        understanding how things work.
      </p>
      <p>
        Leadership has never replaced the part of engineering I enjoy most:
        building systems, experimenting with technology, and working through the
        problems directly.
      </p>
      <h2>The work ahead</h2>
      <p>
        I'm currently focused on agentic software development and secure
        software engineering. I'm interested in the practical details: the
        context an agent needs, the permissions it should have, the evidence
        that a change is correct, and where human judgment belongs.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site is a place to document that work. The{' '}
        <a href={url('projects/')}>projects</a> provide the working context; the{' '}
        <a href={url('writing/')}>field notes</a> are where I work through the
        questions that follow.
      </p>
      <blockquote>
        <p>
          What does software engineering look like when AI agents become
          first-class participants in the development lifecycle?
        </p>
      </blockquote>
      <p>That's the question driving this next chapter.</p>
      <div class="text-links">
        <a href={site.github}>GitHub ↗</a>
        <a href={site.linkedin}>LinkedIn ↗</a>
      </div>
    </article>
    <aside class="about-aside">
      <span class="mono">THE THREAD THROUGH IT ALL</span>
      <ol>
        <li>Software developer</li>
        <li>Architect</li>
        <li>Engineering leader</li>
        <li>Security engineering</li>
        <li>Agentic software development</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="mono">BASED IN ASHEVILLE, NC</p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</Base>
